<title>PERU: Peru's net int'l reserves $8.819 bln on Jan 21.</title>
<headline>Peru's net int'l reserves $8.819 bln on Jan 21.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Tuesday its net international reserves rose to $8.819 billion on January 14 from $8.793 billion the previous week.</p>
<p>Reserves ended 1996 at $8.540 billion.</p>
<p>President Alberto Fujimori said recently the government expected Peru's international reserves to rise above $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
